                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So several different people downvoted the reviewer who called this a Las Vegas Strip simulator.  Guess what?  It's a pretty accurate if simplistic description.  You're in a small apartment (or hotel) and you're shooting people or aliens or cars or whatever down below while some aliens occasionally come walking up to you in your apartment (the cops).  You have an AR (no bump stock) and a sniper rifle to start off.  I think you have unlimited ammo, but I didn't get very far because of my small roomspace.\n\n[b]I played this on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers and it played fine without any problems. [/b] You do need a roomscale setup (small space will suffice) though to grab things around you.  You will need to learn how to reload your gun.  I would practice that after you kill the two aliens coming behind you.  They make a sound when they are near you.  After you die, you go to some type of purgatory.  You can shoot up the place or just go to the door and retry the scenario.\n\nIt's a pixelated world.  But the guns actually felt nice.  The sniper rilfe especially.  You really have to aim properly to get on target.  You can cause quite the mayhem in a short amount of time.  It's nice seeing the vehicles go up on flames.  This is a nice stress reliever for VR for psychopaths. \n\nSale Price Rating 7/10 not bad for $1.49, Normal Price Rating 5.5/10 for $4.99 (not a whole lot of content here) \n\np.s. for those wondering, you teleport around to a few different locations within the apartment",
